      "description": "If Remi Wolf ’s first two albums, 2021’s Juno and 2024’s Big Ideas , were in technicolor, her third LP Mud (out October 9 via Island Records) is more neutral, earthy and grounded. It’s still colorful, as Wolf tends to be, but the newly 30-year-old singer has been on a journey of rooting herself more firmly in the ground. “I feel like I’ve crossed into a new phase of life because of this album,” she says, sitting in the same basement studio at Electric Lady where most of the album was recorded. “I literally felt like I was covered in shit. And now, at the end of the album process, I feel so clean and clear. It has been a very cleansing record to make for me.” The rawness is delivered in the sound: stripped away of synths and programmed drums, Mud is Remi Wolf at her most lyrically and sonically vulnerable. The songs evoke the feeling of singing around a campfire with just your friends and a couple guitars because that’s how it felt for Wolf to make it. But to find the clearing in the fo"
